      {
        "id": 103870,
        "name": "Rabk",
        "username": "Rabk",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabk/{size}/1978_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-20T12:30:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"metlarcturus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/metlarcturus/48/2210_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> metlarcturus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong> Least Favorite:</strong> Slow turns. If I can make and eat a sandwich in the time it takes for my turn to come around again, you’ve pretty much lost me. Especially if there’s no reason to pay attention during other players’ turns.</p><p></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Once the digital version of Brass came out with asynchronous online play in became sooooooo much more fun. Waiting 30 minutes so I can play 2 cards on my turn used to be the worst. Much better when I can get on with my real life while waiting. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=12\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
        "post_number": 327,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:33:06.781Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
