      {
        "id": 103872,
        "name": "BlueHairedMeerkat",
        "username": "BlueHairedMeerkat",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluehairedmeerkat/{size}/1967_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-20T14:09:32.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Least favorite: &nbsp;deck building games. &nbsp;I haven't played one yet that connected theme to gameplay in any meaningful way. &nbsp;They are disguised resource drafting games, I'd rather play Pit.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Might I recommend Mage Knight? Admittedly, it's not a 'pure' deckbuilder, instead integrating deckbuilding into an epic RPG-like experience, but it is a fantastic game, and I find the deck-building element works really well within it.</p>",
